<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zopyrion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 331 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zopyrion was a Macedonian general whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> left as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. Probably around 331 BCE he led a large army against the Getae and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> and besieged the Greek city of Olbia on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. The siege failed, and on the retreat he and his army were destroyed by the Scythians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zopyrion.jpg" alt="Zopyrion" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CristianChirita · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonz_antic_Chisinau_mai_2014_-0065.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
